{"name": "AddAgenda", "description": "Adds an agenda item with specified content, time, and location if a valid, active, and properly formatted user token is provided. The token must start with 'tok-' followed by a non-empty alphanumeric string and must be currently active in the system; correct syntax alone does not guarantee acceptance, as tokens may be expired or deactivated. All parameters — token, content, time, and location — are mandatory and must be non-empty. The time must be a valid UTC datetime in the format '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S', representing an actual point in time (e.g., February 29, 2024 is acceptable; February 30, 2024 is not). Inputs with invalid formats, nonexistent dates, or incorrect time zones (if not pre-converted to UTC) will cause failure. The location and content fields must be valid strings. On success, returns {'status': 'success'}. On any failure — including missing parameters, malformed token, inactive credentials, invalid time format or value, or empty fields — the API raises an explicit exception with a descriptive error message (e.g., 'The token is invalid.'). Clients must validate all inputs for completeness, correctness, and timezone handling, and must implement robust exception handling to manage error responses.", "input_parameters": {"token": {"type": "str", "description": "User's token."}, "content": {"type": "str", "description": "The content of the agenda."}, "time": {"type": "str", "description": "The time for agenda. Format: %Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"}, "location": {"type": "str", "description": "The location of the agenda."}}, "output_parameters": {"status": {"type": "str", "description": "success or failed"}}}
